    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **59 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule for the registration date to skip public holidays in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant with the five fixed dates: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay(...)` from a single-step weekend switch into a loop that rolls the date forward one day at a time while it lands on a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed public holiday \u2014 so it correctly handles cases like a holiday immediately following a weekend (e.g. a Sunday \u2192 Monday holiday chain rolls all the way to the next clear business day).\n\nThis mirrors the reference algorithm the acceptance tests replicate in `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`. The `cp47` holiday-business-day test and the whole suite (59 tests) pass.",
